{%- comment -%}
  Phase 6 — the `snippets/facets.liquid` edit outstanding since Phase 2.

  `facets-horizontal.liquid` renders one dropdown per filter group and calls
  this snippet once per group with `filter:` set. Without the guard below,
  every dropdown renders every filter, so a store with five filters shows
  twenty-five filter groups.

  Two edits, both small.
{%- endcomment -%}


{%- comment -%} ============================================================
  EDIT 1 — the `{%- liquid -%}` block at the top (currently lines 22–25)
  ============================================================ {%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign layout = context | default: 'sidebar'
  assign sort_options = results.sort_options
  assign current_sort = results.sort_by | default: results.default_sort_by

  # A single filter can be passed in, which is how the horizontal layout asks
  # for one group at a time. Wrapping it in an array rather than branching the
  # loop keeps one `{% for %}` below — the alternative duplicates the whole
  # group body, which is 80 lines and the exact duplication this refactor has
  # been removing everywhere else.
  if filter
    assign filters_to_render = filter | concat: empty_array
  else
    assign filters_to_render = results.filters
  endif

  # The horizontal layout supplies its own summary button and popover, so the
  # `<details>` wrapper below would nest a disclosure inside a disclosure.
  assign wrap_in_details = true
  if layout == 'horizontal'
    assign wrap_in_details = false
  endif
-%}


{%- comment -%} ============================================================
  NOTE on `filter | concat: empty_array`

  Liquid has no array literal. `concat` needs an array on both sides, and an
  undefined variable is `nil`, not an empty array — so `filter | concat: nil`
  fails silently and returns nothing.

  If your Liquid version rejects the line above, use this instead, which is
  uglier but works everywhere:

    {%- assign filters_to_render = '' | split: '' -%}
    {%- if filter -%}
      {%- assign filters_to_render = filters_to_render | concat: filter -%}
    {%- endif -%}

  Simplest of all, if you prefer: keep `results.filters` and skip non-matching
  filters inside the loop with

    {%- if filter and f.param_name != filter.param_name -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}

  That costs one wasted iteration per filter and needs no array construction.
  ============================================================ {%- endcomment -%}


{%- comment -%} ============================================================
  EDIT 2 — the filter loop (currently lines 61–71)

  Replace the `{%- for filter in results.filters -%}` line and its `<details>`
  wrapper with the block below. Everything inside `.facets__group-content`
  stays exactly as it is.

  The loop variable is renamed to `f` because `filter` is now the incoming
  parameter, and shadowing it would make the guard above unreadable.
  ============================================================ {%- endcomment -%}

<accordion-element
  class="facets__groups"
  data-collapse-below="{% if layout == 'drawer' %}0{% else %}750{% endif %}"
>
  {%- for f in filters_to_render -%}
    {%- if wrap_in_details -%}
      <details class="facets__group" data-default-open {% if f.active_values.size > 0 %}open{% endif %}>
        <summary class="facets__summary">
          <span class="facets__group-label">{{ f.label }}</span>
          {%- if f.active_values.size > 0 -%}
            <span class="facets__group-count">{{ f.active_values.size }}</span>
          {%- endif -%}
          {% render 'icon', icon: 'chevron-down', size: 14 %}
        </summary>

        <div class="facets__group-content">
          {%- comment -%} …existing filter body, with `filter` renamed to `f`… {%- endcomment -%}
        </div>
      </details>
    {%- else -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Horizontal: no disclosure wrapper, because the dropdown's `<summary>`
        already is one. The body is identical, which is why it should be moved
        into its own snippet rather than written twice — see the note below.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="facets__group facets__group--flat">
        <div class="facets__group-content">
          {%- comment -%} …existing filter body, with `filter` renamed to `f`… {%- endcomment -%}
        </div>
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
</accordion-element>


{%- comment -%} ============================================================
  RECOMMENDED — extract the body

  The filter body is around 80 lines of `{% case filter.type %}` covering price
  ranges, checkboxes and swatches. Pasting it into both branches above means
  the next change to swatch rendering has to be made twice, and the two copies
  will drift the way the carousel branches did.

  Cut everything currently between `<div class="facets__group-content">` and
  its closing tag into `snippets/facet-group.liquid`, taking `filter` and
  `layout` as parameters, then call it from both branches:

    {% render 'facet-group', filter: f, layout: layout, results: results %}

  That is a mechanical move — no logic changes — and it makes the two branches
  above four lines each.
  ============================================================ {%- endcomment -%}
